From 5a3a64044bcd543c7e0434b8d773cf647b64d819 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:34:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: require a completed QMI wait before
 startup

Carry this reviewed SLIMbus/BAM change into maintained Linux 6.18.
Preserve the existing LTS channel-removal/reconfigure protocol, socket
interfaces and DMA provider implementation. This stage is exact patch.

The completed eighteen-change series passes 3,221 source-bound synthetic
cases and 117 independent regression controls, with normal LeakSanitizer
and fail-fast address/undefined-behavior sanitizers. These cover
startup, child and parent ownership, QMI allocation, TX completion
lifetime, synchronous/asynchronous response ownership, DMA admission and
the retained LTS stream caller. Baselines from the appropriate
intermediate stages fail their targeted assertions. All 108 ARM, ARM64
and ARM64 RT component objects build with W=1 and nonpermissive CFI
without diagnostics; their ELF source checksums match the final
candidate.

Kernel waits, workqueues, IDR, PM, packets, DMA and device services in
the host models are synthetic. No real firmware, audio, hardware,
network, phone or installed package executes. Full current-kernel link,
physical DMA-stop/recovery and final-image acceptance remain
unqualified. Codex prepared the LTS adaptations and qualification.
Preserve original authors, dates, notices and assistance credits. Human
DCO and owner, security and subsystem review remain pending; no new
sign-off is added.

Original reviewed changelog and provenance:

The interruptible QMI wait can return a negative error as well as zero
for timeout. Testing only zero lets an interrupted wait continue into
QMI initialization before the service completion has been observed.

Keep the bounded interruptible wait, but continue only for a positive
result. Log an unsuccessful wait without holding the SSR mutex. Seven
synthetic completion outcomes exercise the exact worker callback; the
negative outcomes reproduce the unexpected initialization before this
change. Physical signal delivery and firmware timing are not tested.

OpenAI Codex identified this contract error and implemented the fix,
changelog and host qualification. Human review and DCO are pending.

Fixes: a899d324863a ("slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: add Sub System Restart support")

Backported from commit c506d19f8204 ("slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: require a
completed QMI wait before startup")
---
 drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
index c8e6ebe47f059..1d162bf8599ed 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -1523,13 +1523,15 @@ static void qcom_slim_ngd_down(struct qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl *ctrl)
 static void qcom_slim_ngd_up_worker(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl *ctrl;
+	long ret;
 
 	ctrl = container_of(work, struct qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl, ngd_up_work);
 
 	/* Make sure qmi service is up before continuing */
-	if (!wait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout(&ctrl->qmi_up,
-						       msecs_to_jiffies(MSEC_PER_SEC))) {
-		dev_err(ctrl->dev, "QMI wait timeout\n");
+	ret = wait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout(&ctrl->qmi_up,
+							msecs_to_jiffies(MSEC_PER_SEC));
+	if (ret <= 0) {
+		dev_err(ctrl->dev, "QMI wait failed: %ld\n", ret);
 		return;
 	}
 
